1
00:00:00,074 --> 00:00:02,174
(Man:)It's a shame about those
scientists ripping you off.

2
00:00:02,176 --> 00:00:04,046
(Man:)I expected a higher
ethical standard

3
00:00:04,044 --> 00:00:05,944
(Man:)from our friends in Sweden.

4
00:00:07,615 --> 00:00:09,645
(Leonard:)It's actually pretty common
in our field.

5
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:11,250
(Leonard:)Not much you can do about it.

6
00:00:11,252 --> 00:00:12,752
(Man:)Well, for the right
amount of money,

7
00:00:12,753 --> 00:00:13,953
(Man:)if you know where they live,

8
00:00:13,954 --> 00:00:15,354
(Man:)there's, uh, plenty
we could do about it.

9
00:00:15,356 --> 00:00:17,326
(Sheldon:)Did you hear
that, Leonard?

10
00:00:17,324 --> 00:00:19,954
(Sheldon:)There's plenty we
could do about it.

11
00:00:20,895 --> 00:00:23,865
(Sheldon:)Do you have a card?

12
00:00:25,032 --> 00:00:27,362
(Penny:)Okay, here we go.

13
00:00:27,368 --> 00:00:28,568
(Penny:)Now everyone can see.

14
00:00:28,569 --> 00:00:29,699
(Sheldon:)All right.
(clears throat)

15
00:00:29,703 --> 00:00:32,073
(Penny:)Where do we stand
on cross-eyed Mike?

16
00:00:33,607 --> 00:00:37,307
(Raj:)You know he won't be
looking at other girls.

17
00:00:40,347 --> 00:00:43,287
(Howard:)Unless they're sitting
on the end of his nose.

18
00:00:44,051 --> 00:00:46,181
(Penny:)Okay, okay, okay.
Thumbs down.

19
00:00:46,187 --> 00:00:47,757
(Howard:)Next.

20
00:00:47,755 --> 00:00:49,755
(Bernadette:)Ew, check out
his tiny teeth.

21
00:00:49,757 --> 00:00:51,987
(Bernadette:)He looks like
a man-dolphin.

22
00:00:53,093 --> 00:00:55,893
Wait, if he's good in bed,
she can throw him a fish.

23
00:00:57,298 --> 00:00:58,698
(high-pitched):
I love you, Amy.

24
00:00:58,699 --> 00:01:04,019
(squeaking)

